# Project overview

app-base is a multi-tenant SaaS **template** meant to become a new product: users, full auth (opaque DB session + httpOnly cookie), tenants with members/invites, transactional email, an AI agent (in-app chat + MCP over stdio and HTTP), a platform admin area (`users.isPlatformAdmin` / `PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS` → `/admin`), a public landing page and a one-service deploy on Render (the API serves the built SPA — one origin, simple cookies). The `task` domain is the placeholder resource you copy or replace.

Monorepo (npm workspaces + Turborepo):

- `apps/api` — Hono + Zod + Drizzle/Postgres, organized by domain
- `apps/web` — React 19 + Vite SPA; mirrors the API's domains
- `packages/shared` (`@app/shared`) — Zod input schemas + DTO types imported by both sides
- `packages/ui` (`@app/ui`) — app-neutral base UI (shadcn), imported per subpath

## The golden path

**A feature is a domain folder on both sides.** Never scatter a feature across shared files: it gets its own `apps/api/src/domains/<domain>/` and `apps/web/src/domains/<domain>/`, with its contract in `packages/shared/src/<domain>.ts`. The `task` domain is the canonical example to copy on both sides.

To add a feature/resource end to end, follow the checklist in the `add-feature` skill (`.cursor/skills/add-feature/SKILL.md`).

## Invariants — never break these

- **Tenant isolation**: every resource query filters by `tenantId`. The tenant comes from middleware context (`requireAuth`/`requireTenant`), never from user input. Cross-tenant platform admin queries live only under `/api/admin` gated by `requirePlatformAdmin` — never as a bypass of tenant routes
- **Contracts live in `packages/shared`**: request schemas and DTO types are imported by both API and web — never duplicated on either side
- **Layer boundaries are lint-enforced** (`.oxlintrc.json`): `lib/` imports nothing from the app, `integrations/` only uses `lib/`, domains only know `@/agent/tool` and never import MCP/OpenAI
- **Migrations are generated** from the Drizzle schema (`npm run db:generate`), never hand-written
- **New env var** = add to the Zod schema in `apps/api/src/lib/env.ts` + `.env.example` + `render.yaml`; optional vars must degrade gracefully (like `RESEND_API_KEY` / `OPENAI_API_KEY` do)
- **File naming is fixed**: `<action>.route.ts`, `<action>.tool.ts`, `PascalCasePage.tsx`, kebab-case components; single-role domain files keep the role name (`repository.ts`, `service.ts`); folders own their index (`routes/index.ts` route map, `tools/index.ts` tool list)

## Before finishing any change

Run `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` — both must pass. If you changed a Drizzle schema, run `npm run db:generate` (and `npm run db:migrate` locally).
